{"paper": "RRB-RPF-Constable-12-Mar-2025-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 120, "tagged_count": 34, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Hemant and Irfan can complete a certain piece of work in 9 and 14 days, respectively, They started to work together, and after 3 days, Irfan left. In how many days will Hemant complete the remaining work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Evaluate:", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "roots", "key_answer": "5"}, {"n": 3, "text": "The average of the marks of 14 students in a class is 67. If the marks of each student are doubled, find the new average?", "options": [{"text": "67", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "134", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "134"}, {"n": 4, "text": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 7? a) 171 b) 119 c) 701 d) 387", "options": [{"text": "b", "added": false}, {"text": "c", "added": false}, {"text": "a", "added": false}, {"text": "d", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 5, "text": "Train 1 travelling at a speed of 80 km/hr leaves station A at 6:00 a.m., and train 2 travelling at 105 km/hr starts from station A at 8:30 a.m. in the same direction on a parallel track. At what distance (in km) from station A will train 2 meet train 1?", "options": [{"text": "920", "added": false}, {"text": "840", "added": false}, {"text": "780", "added": false}, {"text": "860", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "840"}, {"n": 6, "text": "If y is the length of the median of an equilateral triangle, then find its area.", "options": [{"text": "2. 2y", "added": false}], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Pipes A and B can fill an empty cistern in 86 minutes and 43 minutes, respectively. Both Pipe A and Pipe B are opened together. After how much time should Pipe A be turned off so that the empty cistern is completely filled in a total of 42 minutes?", "options": [{"text": "20 min", "added": false}, {"text": "15 min", "added": false}, {"text": "5 min", "added": false}, {"text": "2 min", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": "2 min"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The average of first 141 even numbers is", "options": [{"text": "142.5", "added": false}, {"text": "142", "added": false}, {"text": "143", "added": false}, {"text": "141.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": "142"}, {"n": 9, "text": "1% of 93% of a number is what percentage of that number?", "options": [{"text": "0.093", "added": false}, {"text": "94", "added": false}, {"text": "0.93", "added": false}, {"text": "93", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "0.93"}, {"n": 10, "text": "The sum of five numbers is 655. The average of the first two numbers is 78 and the third number is 101. Find the average of the remaining two numbers?", "options": [{"text": "199", "added": false}, {"text": "179", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}, {"text": "200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": "199"}, {"n": 11, "text": "Find HCF of 1826 and 2486.", "options": [{"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "22"}, {"n": 12, "text": "The cost price of an article is 64% of the marked price. Calculate the gain percentage after allowing a discount of 12%.", "options": [{"text": "32.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "47.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "37.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "45.7%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "37.5%"}, {"n": 13, "text": "The sum of five numbers is 655. The average of the first two numbers is 76 and the third number is 108. Find the average of the remaining two numbers?", "options": [{"text": "184", "added": false}, {"text": "198.5", "added": false}, {"text": "197.5", "added": false}, {"text": "185", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": "197.5"}, {"n": 14, "text": "A car travels 209 km in the first hour and 157 km in the second hour. What is the average speed (in km/h) of the car for the whole journey?", "options": [{"text": "179", "added": false}, {"text": "174", "added": false}, {"text": "183", "added": false}, {"text": "193", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "183"}, {"n": 15, "text": "A water tank is in the shape of a cone with a radius of 5 m and a height of 12 m. How much water can the tank hold when full? (Use π ≈ 3.14).", "options": [{"text": "424 m3", "added": false}, {"text": "345 m3", "added": false}, {"text": "327 m3", "added": false}, {"text": "314 m3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": "314 m 3"}, {"n": 16, "text": "A bike goes 32 meters in a second. Find its speed in km/hr.", "options": [{"text": "105.3", "added": false}, {"text": "115.2", "added": false}, {"text": "117.4", "added": false}, {"text": "113.8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "115.2"}, {"n": 17, "text": "The average of X and Y is 40, that of Y and Z is 38, and that of Z and X is 42. Find the average of X, Y and Z.", "options": [{"text": "120", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "40"}, {"n": 18, "text": "Which of the following is the greatest number which divides 1658 and 2041 leaving remainders 7 and 9, respectively?", "options": [{"text": "127", "added": false}, {"text": "135", "added": false}, {"text": "235", "added": false}, {"text": "129", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "remainder-based", "key_answer": "127"}, {"n": 19, "text": "A sum, when invested at 10% simple interest per annum, amounts to ₹2160 after 2 years. What is the simple interest (in ₹) on the same sum at the same rate of interest in 1 year?", "options": [{"text": "360", "added": false}, {"text": "720", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "180"}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "₹1,140"}, {"n": 21, "text": "Mohan purchased a table for ₹2,025 and due to some scratches on its top, he had to sell it for ₹1,675. Find his loss percentage (correct to 